From 7f6f404cd3c2dd83ec6a59a4568053fab30509d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:21:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: expose typed mempool persistence outcomes and exact
 durations

Replace all six legacy producers in kernel/mempool_persist.cpp with
reviewed typed events. Keep their current Info severity, ALL category,
readable messages, evaluation order, exception branches and recovery.
Five import counters have distinct unsigned fields; copy and dump times
retain the existing SecondsDouble intervals and deferred :g rendering.
The copy interval includes the original mutex wait; neither duration is
claimed to measure disk IO alone.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py 0.51.0, run from the parent checkout):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/mempool-persistence.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/mempool-persistence-applied.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/kernel/mempool_persist.cpp

Explicit support: append seven registry keys without changing existing
IDs. Keep the field-list macro's one-entry-per-line style. Add a focused
native JSON/count/precision fixture and one wallet-less functional test
covering missing, valid-empty and corrupt mempool loads, successful dump
and an owned output-directory dump failure. These test additions are
reviewed test code, not claimed to be generated by the conversion script.

Source checks: converter15 fixtures/idempotence, production event lint297,
Ruff0.15.8 and diff whitespace pass. Native compilation and actual new
functional behavior are pending and recorded separately; no suite or
benchmark pass is claimed. Shared eCash owner; V2 inherits unchanged.
